{:edb/db-before-t 1543 :edb/db-after-t 1544 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534856 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:08:24.445Z" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186107321 1078 #edb/ref 17592186107324 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186107465 1078 #edb/ref 17592186107468 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110295 1071 "![](images/2f/2f6d703c604c780da8c97a012b94e75f06a55aa8b6e706a1097dc33ff193e88c.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The points $K$, $N$, and $Z$ are collinear\n2. The points $K$, $P$, and $J$ are collinear" 13194139534856 17592186045417 false] [17592186110295 1071 "![](images/2f/2f6d703c604c780da8c97a012b94e75f06a55aa8b6e706a1097dc33ff193e88c.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The points $K$, $N$, and $Z$ are collinear\n\nII. The points $K$, $P$, and $J$ are collinear" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110674 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441206 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110674 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441209 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110674 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441210 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110674 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441212 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110675 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441205 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110675 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441207 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110675 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441208 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110675 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441211 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110859 1050 420.0 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110905 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110905 1071 "![](images/36/36ea34524b2ca277e8061441492711d36c8065e765d519d85d4008da97c3f8b3.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\n1. $M, N, R$\n2. $P, S, T$\n3. $O, P, S$" 13194139534856 17592186045417 false] [17592186110905 1071 "![](images/36/36ea34524b2ca277e8061441492711d36c8065e765d519d85d4008da97c3f8b3.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,N,R$\n\nII. $P,S,T$\n\nIII. $O,P,S$" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110905 1074 "- $M,N,R$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/b8/b8fae613772422b14fce2e2db0762f659599f0b17409223ec291802b5d760d9c.png)\n\n- $P,S,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/85/85638c1466360f3e5285c34e84903824140b9e2fc72a0f029ab1ded170b64eb2.png)\n\n- $O,P,S$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/4b/4b7ef30e306e3c7e70dadb1524e1f60a9ea01832215009ef2ea8344cb07e7297.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110929 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186110929 1074 "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/54/54735541d4dfc424fe186ddabe0c3f9d3cbd45a0dc7a1b8f4551cf8c5e5bc14f.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/f0/f00f882c97fd201178e54f29151a48a4f41d4108cf375104cc338e968c55761b.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/6e/6e0c0320775d93364e32655d1e09081382078fa7e96fbe621a8c558f63dfcabb.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186111906 1064 "For any two distinct points, there is always one (and only one) line that passes through them.\n\nFor example, the line passing through the points $P$ and $Q$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{PQ}$, while the line that passes through $A$ and $B$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{AB}$:\n\n![](images/8c/8c79a551e7ced71de157ea292baa3d7f38afaca4ea76ee467fc4add1b28ed33f.png)\n\nHowever, given three or more points, there is not always a line that passes through all of them.\n\nFor example, for the three points $F, G$, and $H$ below, it is impossible to draw a single straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/30/30361c0bd49e571e317746f2d88848626da52e5ddbcda8fe9b6f496e4aff6b69.png)\n\nHowever, it is *sometimes* possible to draw a line through three (or more) points. In such cases, we say that the points are **collinear**.\n\nFor example, the points $M$, $N$, and $O$ shown below are collinear since they all lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/bf/bf3de55518c21de30718b2d9fee7032139c89aa3a4a963b8346b457ceafbeada.png)" 13194139534856 17592186045417 false] [17592186111906 1064 "For any two distinct points, there is always one (and only one) line that passes through them.\n\nFor example, the line passing through the points $P$ and $Q$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{PQ},$ while the line that passes through $A$ and $B$ is $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/8c/8c79a551e7ced71de157ea292baa3d7f38afaca4ea76ee467fc4add1b28ed33f.png)\n\nHowever, given three or more points, there is not always a line that passes through all of them.\n\nFor example, for the three points $F, G,$ and $H$ below, it is impossible to draw a single straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/30/30361c0bd49e571e317746f2d88848626da52e5ddbcda8fe9b6f496e4aff6b69.png)\n\nHowever, it is *sometimes* possible to draw a line through three (or more) points. In such cases, we say that the points are **collinear**.\n\nFor example, the points $M,$ $N,$ and $O$ shown below are collinear since they all lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/bf/bf3de55518c21de30718b2d9fee7032139c89aa3a4a963b8346b457ceafbeada.png)" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441157 1080 "II only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441157 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441157 1083 #uuid "004b80fe-aa14-5965-b4ca-127d549ed72f" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441158 1080 "I and II only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441158 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441158 1083 #uuid "02057e88-897b-5572-b38e-d69c819eeed3" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441159 1080 "I and II only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441159 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441159 1083 #uuid "09c250ea-692c-547e-a705-4dc418eb0270" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441160 1080 "I only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441160 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441160 1083 #uuid "0ad41565-a704-532b-bb33-f22b0b4d71bc" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441161 1080 "I and II only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441161 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441161 1083 #uuid "11c7107d-7a3f-5c78-b66e-f38c1897d9ec" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441162 1080 "I only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441162 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441162 1083 #uuid "26034fca-f6aa-5214-becb-da1b7bcfc8fa" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441163 1080 "III only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441163 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441163 1083 #uuid "2930bce2-2f13-5db1-a8f1-ab9025f0839b" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441164 1080 "I only" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441164 1082 #edb/ref