true] [17592186441209 1069 "q-7506" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441209 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441209 1071 "![](images/ff/ff66db91618a2b238e99a86d5a896948e9d7b012774ee98a3f06051c1f7862bd.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $C,$ $D,$ and $F$ are **not** collinear\n\nII. $D,$ $E,$ and $H$ are **not** collinear\n\nIII. $A,$ $B,$ and $F$ are collinear" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441209 1072 #uuid "3b296615-3f48-5786-b13b-e934d75d7ab2" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441209 1074 "- Statement I is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/4e/4efadc7686e7d8845c98d97e16c44a19d233ae5ef50df160ce12b1823725966d.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/da/da1fb5e45ddfc41a8a9ff592ade9e5f2d5411e07b8e6ed1cf4ddad7e5841f6ae.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/4f/4fd5a2ee4afd7c9d61b4d8e20cf676c602167d1d8f21a6392f36bcfeb54a8f25.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441210 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441202 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441210 1069 "q-13447" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441210 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441210 1071 "![](images/50/50dfc42742418eae8eb25f26fd193b714e06b820f99945ac2b8b759eed3a349e.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $Q,S,T$\n\nII. $M,O,Q$\n\nIII. $N,P,T$" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441210 1072 #uuid "3c2f5f2a-936e-5967-a391-3ffba6cfe5b2" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441210 1074 "- $Q,S,T$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/21/2101dd8ae066aa55d601263de389e013100e476ddbf5220381e4040440b344a9.png)\n\n- $M,O,Q$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/d2/d29ca68ff7123964944eded292ec8ea2c6b16a9fd46e875472e7666f114c8cad.png)\n\n- $N,P,T$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](images/03/03db0865e93c7c9a1a2f1c23fd8027602e04299903edb6996b9f0b2150d1d036.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441211 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441199 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441211 1069 "q-154974" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441211 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441211 1071 "![](images/f5/f5678237a4e3448f737500d08159b916317940cd427be6c9d65e5647fb007068.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams above shows three collinear points?" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441211 1072 #uuid "80288dbc-4d6c-56f8-bd9c-a2e8f0f4201b" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441211 1074 "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/64/64de4db5f989920ef14340ff7e218fbad9460ae836f2e4c50450b30fc2867f07.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/01/013d1ac170724461fd35cc1d29a4ce455890537543b362c2e9f193c3f2a92df9.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/60/60489a11b93b0f55965251fc739a77dee62a962519143fa0b17d53c0e35200b2.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441212 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441198 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441212 1069 "q-13444" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441212 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441212 1071 "![](images/e9/e9ede3d8d40b90fcf4919b85917c2fa21bf91163d136a1cd40b8bd6c0db3b40d.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. Point $K$ is **not** collinear with the points $M$ and $N$\n\nII. Points $L,O,Q$ are collinear\n\nIII. Points $J,K,Q$ are **not** collinear" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441212 1072 #uuid "b615808c-9716-5264-afdc-7e0ca61bc6d9" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true] [17592186441212 1074 "- Statement I is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/fa/fa3ac1e9323a72254ecfc2242b1de23c05f0cc639b593eeadacb64ed6b4d4036.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/88/8895800b4c1ca6d22d42fac0cdb1488f716bdb5b59b49496d2f908f0947314b0.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/f3/f39a0462a8a52762c7525e31746e69269ab4b9521f4cc4e8121b114e98ddb68a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534856 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-004b80fe-aa14-5965-b4ca-127d549ed72f" 17592186441157 "answer-02057e88-897b-5572-b38e-d69c819eeed3" 17592186441158 "answer-09c250ea-692c-547e-a705-4dc418eb0270" 17592186441159 "answer-0ad41565-a704-532b-bb33-f22b0b4d71bc" 17592186441160 "answer-11c7107d-7a3f-5c78-b66e-f38c1897d9ec" 17592186441161 "answer-26034fca-f6aa-5214-becb-da1b7bcfc8fa" 17592186441162 "answer-2930bce2-2f13-5db1-a8f1-ab9025f0839b" 17592186441163 "answer-2afe9ef2-fa5d-58e2-a13f-ad84913f8e2a" 17592186441164 "answer-31ca891c-5736-5088-847e-9d8792be5463" 17592186441165 "answer-339b3426-cf16-5642-a40a-711c00b84dee" 17592186441166 "answer-39cd6397-aa4f-5006-bf7d-9045dbc70482" 1759218644